  "presentation_summary": [
    "29-year-old man presented after 7 days of fever and developed confusion, restlessness, and urinary incontinence on the day of admission.",
    "He had travel to southern Saudi Arabia, appeared pale and jaundiced, had GCS 12/15 without meningitis signs, pulse 120/min, BP 90/50 mmHg, RR 20/min, and temperature 36.9 C.",
    "Initial labs showed WBC 9.9 x10^9/L and platelets 12 x10^9/L; blood film showed P. falciparum ring forms with parasitemia greater than 5%.",
    "Hemolysis was severe with bilirubin 208 micromol/L, reticulocyte count 375 x10^9/L (11%), LDH 2197 U/L, haptoglobin 0.07 g/L, and hemoglobin dropping to 4 g/dL requiring blood transfusion.",
    "Two days after admission, creatinine rose to 167 micromol/L and urea to 17.6 mmol/L; CRP was 215 mg/L and ferritin 2852 ng/mL.",
    "On admission day 3 he developed cough and shortness of breath with bilateral infiltrates; ABG showed PaO2 55.6 mmHg on FiO2 32% and PaO2/FiO2 ratio 174.",
    "He received IV artesunate, blood transfusion, and high-flow oxygen support with slow parasite clearance over 10 days."
  ],
